# Resched.me: Scaffold → Production Implementation Plan

## Current State Assessment

The codebase is a **well-structured scaffold** with the right architectural bones but **zero working integrations**:

| Layer | What exists | What's missing |
|-------|------------|----------------|
| **Backend routes** | 6 route files (auth, calendar, ai, scheduling, voice, vision) | All return hardcoded mock data |
| **Models** | [User](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/models/user.py#9-16), [EnergyProfile](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/models/energy_profile.py#10-24), [CalendarConnection](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/models/calendar_connection.py#9-22) with SQLAlchemy | No migrations, no CRUD operations used |
| **Services** | 5 service files with function stubs | No OpenAI, Whisper, Google Calendar, or OCR calls |
| **Auth** | Google OAuth URL builder only | No callback, no token exchange, no JWT, no session |
| **Frontend** | Landing page with 3 components | No routing, no API calls, no auth, no real calendar |
| **Infra** | Docker Compose with Postgres + Redis | No Alembic, no Redis usage, uses `create_all` |

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This plan assumes you can provide the following secrets before Phase 1 begins:
> - **Google Cloud Console**: OAuth 2.0 Client ID + Secret (with Calendar API enabled)
> - **OpenAI API key** (for gpt-4o-mini and Whisper API access)

> [!WARNING]
> Phase 1 (Google Calendar) is a **hard dependency** for Phases 2–5. We cannot demo real calendar writes until the OAuth flow works end-to-end.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Build order matters.** The phases below are designed so each one produces a demo-able milestone. I recommend tackling them in order (0→8), but feel free to request changes to priority.

---

