## Phase 1 — Google OAuth + Calendar Integration

> **Goal:** Users can sign in with Google, and the app can read/write their Google Calendar events with an approval workflow.

#### [MODIFY] [auth.py](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/api/routes/auth.py)
- Add `GET /auth/google/callback` — exchange code for tokens, create/upsert user, store encrypted Google tokens, return JWT
- Add `GET /auth/me` — return current user profile
- Add `POST /auth/logout` — revoke session

#### [MODIFY] [calendar_connection.py](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/models/calendar_connection.py)
- Add `access_token`, `refresh_token`, `token_expires_at` encrypted columns

#### [NEW] `apps/api/app/services/google_calendar.py`
- Wrapper around Google Calendar API v3 using `httpx`
- Functions: `list_events()`, [create_event()](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/api/routes/calendar.py#14-17), `update_event()`, `delete_event()`
- Automatic token refresh on 401

#### [MODIFY] [calendar.py (service)](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/services/calendar.py)
- Replace hardcoded mocks with calls to `google_calendar.py`
- Add approval status tracking (pending → approved → synced)

#### [MODIFY] [calendar.py (route)](file:///c:/Users/kuday/reschedai/apps/api/app/api/routes/calendar.py)
- Add `PUT /events/{id}`, `DELETE /events/{id}`
- Add `POST /events/{id}/approve` — approval workflow trigger
- Protect all routes with `get_current_user` dependency

#### Frontend changes
#### [NEW] `apps/web/src/app/login/page.tsx`
- Google sign-in button, redirect to Google OAuth URL from API

#### [NEW] `apps/web/src/lib/auth.ts`
- Auth context provider, token storage (localStorage + httpOnly cookie consideration), `useAuth()` hook

#### [NEW] `apps/web/src/components/auth-guard.tsx`
- Protected route wrapper redirecting unauthenticated users to `/login`

